  "source_changes": {
    "runtime": "Remove the process-environment early return from video_adapter_init. The existing adapter callback, GM20B NVDEC resources and client checks, and 128000-byte firmware verification then run for eligible processes. An eligible adapter offers the D3D11.1 interface through GetSupportedVersions.",
    "hardware_start": "The adapter query copies the start-time KMD resource/client snapshot. Firmware upload to the engine starts in CreateVideoDecoder; capability discovery reads and verifies the firmware on the CPU.",
    "other_source": "The ARM64 test fixture stops setting the video opt-in. The package updater accepts a default-enabled UMD and clears obsolete selection metadata.",
    "prior_kernel_change": {
      "commit": "8e9f265f7d0ebb9deab6b57dd576d76e2d0c736f",
      "scope": "A high-resolution one-shot timer polls pending GPU fences. The unchanged signed kernel was used in both comparison arms."
    },
    "presentation_hypothesis": "CreateDevice prepares the runtime-device NVK submission transport for the Win7 DDI, and for a D3D11.1 video device only with the separate window diagnostic request. Ordinary D3D11.1 callers can negotiate a different path. Existing resource contract tests demonstrate a displayable-resource failure without runtime-queue ownership. The UMD hash loaded by DWM identifies the binary; it does not identify the DDI selected by DWM or prove the cause of a system reset.",
