  "decision": "The original gate-only aebab8b0 and the manually interrupted comparison remain historical. The accepted ded6fa4a package combines default video discovery with checked completion and retirement. Continue objective 5 before investigating high-load restarts in objective 4.",
  "independent_submission_sync": {
    "scope": "Trace the skip path while retaining default H.264 capability discovery. The repair was built from the same frozen source as the candidate and keeps the D3D11.1 runtime-queue selection unchanged.",
    "ordinary_submission": "The D3D runtime signals the ingress monitored fence. NVK waits on the imported ingress payload and signals its completion fence. The D3D runtime queues a wait on that completion value. The independent NVK context opens the fence through the NT handle; the runtime-owned context instead retains the explicit owner token.",
    "low_level_wait": "The normal independent KMT semaphore wait re-reads the mapped fence value. The CPU fixture deliberately supplies an inconsistent successful Vulkan wait to check the outer UMD contract. The available hardware traces have no recorded example of that inconsistency.",
    "cleanup_difference": "The frozen UMD trusted a successful Vulkan wait even if a second counter read was below the target, and forced retirement after an inconclusive native DeviceWaitIdle in independent-context teardown. The branch already contains checked wait and deferred teardown commit ccfc48f4a32c890bede65bd8b07af61d68aa0eea. Both originally compared UMDs were built without that retirement delta.",
